## 4. CI and CD
 
### CI — Continuous Integration
Automatically **builds and tests** code on every push/PR:
- Compile the code
- Run unit/integration tests
- Check code style / linting
- Run static analysis (e.g. SonarQube)
### CD — Continuous Delivery / Deployment
Extends CI by also **deploying** the artifact:
- **Continuous Delivery** — auto-deploys to staging; human approves push to production
- **Continuous Deployment** — fully automated all the way to production
### "It's only CI"
Means the pipeline **stops after testing** — nothing is deployed automatically. Common when:
- The project is early-stage
- Deployment is handled separately or manually
- The repo is a library, not a deployable service
