## 5. Spring Boot Application Structure
 
```
src/
└── main/
    └── java/com/yourcompany/appname/
        ├── AppNameApplication.java   ← Main class
        ├── controller/
        ├── service/
        ├── repository/
        ├── model/  (entities)
        ├── dto/
        └── config/
```
 
### Main Class
```java
@SpringBootApplication
public class AppNameApplication {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(AppNameApplication.class, args);
    }
}
```
`@SpringBootApplication` combines `@Configuration` + `@EnableAutoConfiguration` + `@ComponentScan`.
 
### Layer Responsibilities
 
| Layer | Annotation | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| Controller | `@RestController` | Handles HTTP, calls service, returns response. No business logic. |
| Service | `@Service` | All business logic. Calls repositories. |
| Repository | `@Repository` | Talks to the database. Extends `JpaRepository`. |
| Entity/Model | `@Entity` | Maps to a database table. |
| DTO | Plain class | Shapes data for the API. Keeps DB model separate from API. |
| Config | `@Configuration` | Security, CORS, beans, etc. |
 
### Request Flow
```
HTTP Request
    ↓
Controller        ← validates input, handles routing
    ↓
Service           ← business logic
    ↓
Repository        ← database query
    ↓
Database
 
Model = DB shape | DTO = API shape
```
 
