## 9. Schema Definition and Data Seeding
 
### SAP Commerce Cloud → Spring Boot equivalents
 
| SAP Commerce Cloud | Spring Boot |
|---|---|
| `items.xml` (schema definition) | `@Entity` classes + `ddl-auto`, or `schema.sql` |
| `items.xml` (schema evolution) | Flyway / Liquibase |
| Impex (data seeding) | `data.sql`, Flyway, or `CommandLineRunner` |
 
### ddl-auto options
```yaml
spring:
  jpa:
    hibernate:
      ddl-auto: update
```
 
| Value | Behaviour |
|---|---|
| `create` | Drop and recreate on every startup |
| `update` | Add missing columns/tables, don't drop |
| `create-drop` | Create on start, drop on shutdown |
| `validate` | Check schema matches entities, no changes |
| `none` | Do nothing |
 
### schema.sql
```
src/main/resources/schema.sql
```
Spring Boot runs this automatically on startup.
 
### Flyway (recommended for production)
Versioned SQL migration files:
```
src/main/resources/db/migration/
    V1__create_users_table.sql
    V2__add_bio_to_users.sql
```
Each file runs **once and never again** — Flyway tracks what's been applied.
 
