## 11. MapStruct and Bean Mapping
 
### Before MapStruct — Manual Mapping
```java
public static CommentDto toDto(CommentEntity entity) {
    CommentDto dto = new CommentDto();
    dto.setId(entity.getId());
    dto.setBody(entity.getBody());
    return dto;
}
```
 
**Problems:**
- Extremely tedious for many fields
- Silent bugs when you add a field — compiler won't warn you
- Mapping logic scattered across services
### BeanUtils
```java
BeanUtils.copyProperties(source, destination);
```
Copies fields by matching names at **runtime via reflection**.
 
**Problems:**
- Different field names silently skipped
- Type mismatches cause runtime errors, not compile-time
- No IDE support
### MapStruct
Generates mapping code at **compile time**:
 
```java
@Mapper(componentModel = "spring")
public interface CommentMapper {
 
    @Mapping(source = "author.username", target = "authorName")
    CommentDto toDto(CommentEntity entity);
 
    @Mapping(target = "author", ignore = true)
    CommentEntity toEntity(CommentDto dto);
}
```
 
MapStruct generates the implementation automatically. You inject and use it:
 
```java
@Service
public class CommentsService {
    private final CommentMapper commentMapper;
 
    public ResponseEntity<Comment> getComment(Long id) {
        CommentEntity entity = commentRepository.findById(id);
        Comment dto = commentMapper.toDto(entity);
        return ResponseEntity.ok(dto);
    }
}
```
 
### Comparison
 
| | Manual | BeanUtils | MapStruct |
|---|---|---|---|
| Boilerplate | Tons | Minimal | Minimal |
| Compile-time safety | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ |
| Performance | Fast | Slow (reflection) | Fast (generated code) |
| New field added | Silent bug | Silent bug | Build error |
| Enterprise use | Small projects | Occasional | Very common |
 
> Further reading: [Baeldung — MapStruct](https://www.baeldung.com/mapstruct)
 
